 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Service Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a service landing page?\", \"a\": \"A service landing page is a single web page that sells one service, such as a furnace repair or a lawn mowing plan, and asks the visitor to request it. It carries the offer, the area served, the price or how pricing works, and one form or call button, with nothing that leads away from the request.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a service landing page?\", \"a\": \"Pick the one service the page sells and list the ZIP codes you cover, then describe both to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, along with who should hear about each request. Emergent builds the page and the database behind it from that prompt, and you change the offer or the form later by prompting again.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a landing page for my service business ask visitors to do?\", \"a\": \"Ask for one thing: a request for the service the page sells, or a phone call. Match the action to how the job gets scheduled. A fixed-price visit can be booked straight from the form, while a job that needs an estimate should end in a request for one. Keep a second, competing button off the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes the best landing page for a service business?\", \"a\": \"One job, one service area, and a plain next step make the best page: a price or an estimate, a short form, and a phone number. Write one page per service, not one for the whole company. A general <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/business'>business landing page</a> suits offers that are not a single job, such as wholesale orders or catering.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do the strongest landing page examples for services have in common?\", \"a\": \"Each of the four examples above sells one job and runs one rule behind its form: a ZIP code check, a price per visit, a route to the right person, or a cap on bookings per Saturday. When you study any service page, look for that rule first. It decides what happens after the visitor presses the button.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a tree service landing page include?\", \"a\": \"Include the jobs the crew does, such as removal, trimming, or stump grinding, as separate choices on the form, plus the ZIP codes you cover. Ask where the tree stands and whether it is near the house or power lines; the estimator needs both before the site visit. Photos of finished jobs from your own crew do more than stock images.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I write a service landing page that sells to other companies?\", \"a\": \"Name the business result in the headline, show the scope of the service and the kind of company it suits, and end with one request, such as a site visit or a call. Put the commercial details on the page too, like the hours your crews work and how you invoice. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/b2b'>b2b landing page</a> covers longer buying decisions with several people involved.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do I need a separate service landing page for each service I offer?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when you send ads or mailers to that service. A visitor who searched for gutter cleaning should see gutter cleaning first. Keep a combined services page on your main site for browsing. Emergent builds each page from its own prompt, and every page's requests land in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I track which ads bring requests to my service business landing page?\", \"a\": \"Give each ad its own link with a campaign tag, and add a hidden field to the form that saves that tag with the request. Count requests by tag each week and cut the ads that send none. Requests from a page Emergent builds are stored in a database you own, and each row carries the tag beside the request details.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I send people from a printed flyer to my service landing page?\", \"a\": \"Print a QR code and a short web address that open the page for the one service on the flyer, not your home page. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/qr-code'>qr code landing page</a> is read on a phone. Keep its first screen light: web.dev says sites should strive to have Largest Contentful Paint of 2.5 seconds or less. Repeat the offer from the print at the top.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 },
